  "review_notes": [
    "Corrected in chapter reconciliation: the supplied 'even' was folded into the appositional lamed's unit, which now holds 'even for' headed on 'for'. The verse pass had left it added under rule 16's appositional sentence, but that sentence governs a phrase on which no morpheme stands, and this lamed stands on the very phrase the 'even' introduces. 2CH.26.12 aligns the same appositional lamed to a bare 'even' and 2CH.26.8 keeps 'even to' whole on the preposition, so the added reading was the chapter's one unlicensed difference.",
    "'coats of mail' was headed on 'mail' by rule 31's subtraction; heading on 'coats' was the competing reading.",
    "The written 'for' before 'slinging' was given to the construct relation rather than to the phrase-initial lamed; the reverse allocation, leaving the rectum bare, was the competing reading. The lamed of s006 takes its words because the ASV writes them at that phrase's left edge, which is the same test."
